<script lang="ts">import { resolve } from '$app/paths'; import ReviewControlsFigure from '$lib/docs/ReviewControlsFigure.svelte'; import DocsDiagram from '$lib/docs/DocsDiagram.svelte';</script>
<svelte:head><title>Review, versions & sharing · Review Room</title><meta name="description" content="See how feedback, versions, current picks and sharing fit together." /></svelte:head>
<header class="docs-heading"><p class="docs-kicker">Using Review Room</p><h1>Watch the take.<br />Make the decision clear.</h1><p class="docs-lead">Feedback belongs to the asset. Creative details belong to the take. Sharing is a separate choice.</p></header>
<DocsDiagram kind="review" caption="Changing the current pick keeps the other takes. Comments are asset-level: include the take label in a note when the version matters." />
<section id="review-controls"><h2>Three places to look</h2><ReviewControlsFigure /></section>
<section class="docs-instructions" id="feedback"><h2>Leave and handle feedback</h2><ol class="docs-steps"><li>Open an asset and check its version. Pause video at the moment you want to discuss.</li><li>Open <strong>Notes & info → Notes</strong>. Type a note; keep the timecode checked for a moment-specific comment, or uncheck it for a general note.</li><li>Use <strong>Add note</strong>. Wait for it to appear in the note list. A draft is not saved feedback.</li><li>Use <strong>Request changes</strong> or <strong>Approve</strong> for the decision. The owner follows outstanding notes in the feedback inbox and marks handled feedback complete.</li></ol><p>For still images, expand the preview to draw, undo, clear and save markup. Saved markup does not modify the original image.</p></section>
<section class="docs-instructions" id="versions"><h2>Inspect a take, make it current, or add a revision</h2><p>The <strong>Asset version</strong> menu chooses the take you inspect. If it differs from the saved pick, <strong>Make current</strong> selects it as current without deleting other takes or changing existing publications.</p><p>In <strong>Fields</strong>, edit the selected version’s prompt, model, notes and image references, then <strong>Save version metadata</strong>. A concurrent-save conflict keeps the draft; reload and reconcile before saving again.</p><p>For an existing video publication, use <strong>Publish & share → Video embeds → New version</strong>. Creative Studio Pro can add takes by code through the API or filename matching in managed folders. A separate ordinary upload creates a separate asset.</p></section>
<section id="sharing"><h2>Choose an audience</h2><DocsDiagram kind="sharing" caption="These are separate permission paths. A new upload stays private. Making a take current does not automatically update a published version." /></section>
<section class="docs-instructions" id="private-review"><h2>Private review: invite people to watch and comment</h2><ol class="docs-steps"><li>Open <strong>Publish & share → Private review</strong>.</li><li>Choose the project, optional passcode, expiry and download permission. Use <strong>Create private link</strong> and copy the result for the intended reviewers. This control creates project-wide links.</li><li>Reviewers can watch, comment, rate, shortlist and make supported review decisions. Downloads need both link permission and enabled asset downloads.</li><li><strong>Revoke</strong> withdraws access. Expired or revoked links cannot become public embeds or permanent media URLs.</li></ol><figure class="docs-visual docs-sharing-figure"><img class="docs-screenshot" src="/docs/images/private-sharing-20261026-2x.png" alt="Private review controls: project, passcode, expiry and separate link/asset download permissions." width="960" height="1300" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The first checkbox allows downloads through this link. The second allows the chosen asset to be downloaded. Both must be enabled. Creating this link does not publish to Trailer Feed.</figcaption></figure><p>Review links do not grant folder management, archive or production deletion controls.</p></section>
<section class="docs-instructions" id="publication"><h2>Trailer Feed: publish exact ready versions</h2><p>Open <strong>Publish & share → Destinations</strong> and connect an ordinary project or folder. <strong>All videos</strong> selects current unsynced videos for one confirmation; <strong>Choose versions</strong> pins individual takes. Check included images and authorize the exact public selection, then <strong>Publish all videos</strong> or <strong>Sync selected versions</strong>. This explicit consent does not require approval status.</p><p>Later uploads remain private. Trailer Feed assigns project-local version numbers in selected-version creation order, oldest first. Source asset codes/version IDs remain the integration identity.</p><div class="docs-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Refresh metadata</td><td>Fills empty target fields and preserves deliberate target edits and existing media URLs. New images need consent.</td></tr><tr><td>Unsync</td><td>Withdraws delivery while preserving source media and feedback. Ordinary retries cannot resurrect it.</td></tr><tr><td>Sync again</td><td>Requires fresh confirmation after disconnection.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Locked Creative Studio Pro folders cannot connect directly. <strong>Copy to folder</strong> creates an independent asset in an ordinary folder while sharing stored bytes; connect that folder.</p></section>
<section class="docs-instructions" id="embeds"><h2>Video embeds and ordered showcases</h2><p><strong>Video embeds</strong> publishes an approved, ready video version to exact allowed HTTPS site origins. <strong>Replace at URL</strong> changes the eligible version while retaining the slug; <strong>Revoke</strong> disables it. <strong>Showcase</strong> combines published videos in a chosen order. These controls are separate from private reviews and Trailer Feed sync.</p></section>
